{
  "name": "Webhook response modes + Wait for approval",
  "meta": {
    "description": "Three small workflows to show the webhook response modes (respond immediately with a custom status and body, respond with the output of the last node) and a Wait node that pauses a run until an approval link is opened, even across a server restart. The REST API example shows the third mode (Respond to Webhook node).",
    "categories": [
      "Webhooks",
      "Utilities"
    ]
  },
  "workflows": [
    {
      "key": "immediate",
      "name": "Webhook: respond immediately",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "Webhook",
          "type": "flowforge.webhook",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "path": "demo/immediate",
            "httpMethod": "POST",
            "responseMode": "onReceived",
            "options": {
              "responseCode": 201,
              "responseBody": "{\"accepted\": true}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "Save order",
          "type": "flowforge.set",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            240,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "includeOtherFields": false,
            "assignments": {
              "assignments": [
                {
                  "id": "a",
                  "name": "order",
                  "value": "={{ $json.body.item }}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "note-0",
          "name": "How to try it",
          "type": "flowforge.stickyNote",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            -260
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "content": "## Respond immediately\n1. Toggle **Active**.\n2. Open the Webhook node and copy the **Production URL**.\n3. `curl -X POST <url> -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"item\":\"book\"}'`\n\nThe caller gets **201** and `{\"accepted\": true}` at once, while the workflow keeps running.",
            "width": 420,
            "height": 200,
            "color": 4
          }
        }
      ],
      "connections": {
        "Webhook": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Save order",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "lastnode",
      "name": "Webhook: respond with the last node",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "Webhook",
          "type": "flowforge.webhook",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "path": "demo/last-node",
            "httpMethod": "POST",
            "responseMode": "lastNode",
            "responseData": "firstEntryJson"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "Greet",
          "type": "flowforge.set",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            240,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "assignments": {
              "assignments": [
                {
                  "id": "a",
                  "name": "greeting",
                  "value": "=Hello {{ $json.body.name }}!",
                  "type": "string"
                },
                {
                  "id": "b",
                  "name": "length",
                  "value": "={{ $json.body.name.length }}",
                  "type": "number"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "note-0",
          "name": "How to try it",
          "type": "flowforge.stickyNote",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            -260
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "content": "## Respond when the last node finishes\n1. Toggle **Active**, copy the **Production URL**.\n2. `curl -X POST <url> -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"name\":\"Ada\"}'`\n\nThe answer is the output of the last node: `Hello Ada!`.",
            "width": 420,
            "height": 200,
            "color": 4
          }
        }
      ],
      "connections": {
        "Webhook": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Greet",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "wait",
      "name": "Wait for approval (webhook resume)",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "Webhook",
          "type": "flowforge.webhook",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "path": "demo/approval",
            "httpMethod": "POST",
            "responseMode": "onReceived",
            "options": {
              "responseBody": "={\"message\": \"Waiting for approval\"}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "Remember resume URL",
          "type": "flowforge.set",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            240,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "includeOtherFields": true,
            "assignments": {
              "assignments": [
                {
                  "id": "a",
                  "name": "approveUrl",
                  "value": "={{ $execution.resumeUrl }}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "name": "Wait for approval",
          "type": "flowforge.wait",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            480,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "resume": "webhook",
            "httpMethod": "GET"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "4",
          "name": "Approved",
          "type": "flowforge.set",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            720,
            0
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "assignments": {
              "assignments": [
                {
                  "id": "a",
                  "name": "decision",
                  "value": "={{ $json.query.decision }}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "note-0",
          "name": "How to try it",
          "type": "flowforge.stickyNote",
          "typeVersion": 1,
          "position": [
            0,
            -260
          ],
          "parameters": {
            "content": "## Wait for approval (survives a restart)\n1. Toggle **Active**, call the webhook (POST).\n2. The run **waits**: see it in **Executions**.\n3. Open the resume URL from the run (`approveUrl`) with `?decision=yes`.\n\nYou can stop and restart FlowForge in between: the run still resumes.",
            "width": 420,
            "height": 200,
            "color": 4
          }
        }
      ],
      "connections": {
        "Webhook": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Remember resume URL",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Remember resume URL": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Wait for approval",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        "Wait for approval": {
          "main": [
            [
              {
                "node": "Approved",
                "type": "main",
                "index": 0
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}